{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 420,
    "dDurationMs": 3890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Matter is everywhere: we eat it, breathe it,\ndrink it; it is who we are."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4310,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But what is matter?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5810,
    "dDurationMs": 4340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The most basic particle physics definition\nof matter comes down to one surprising rule:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10150,
    "dDurationMs": 4740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Pauli exclusion principle - or, essentially,\nelectrons hate being alike."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14890,
    "dDurationMs": 4250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To understand why, we have to remember the\nfact that every electron is exactly the same."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19140,
    "dDurationMs": 2130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Not \"kind of the same\"…"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21270,
    "dDurationMs": 1690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They're perfectly identical."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22960,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just as you can at anytime, anywhere, spontaneously\nwrite down the number three and it will mean"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27880,
    "dDurationMs": 4769,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "exactly, perfectly, three… as if there were\nsome everywhere-permeating \"three-ness\" always"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 32649,
    "dDurationMs": 2030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "available to produce a three at your whim."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34679,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's the same case with the electron: there's\nan everywhere-permeating \"electron-ness\" called"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39639,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a \"quantum field,\" and from that field every\nelectron in existence has been summoned, and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 44359,
    "dDurationMs": 2491,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they are all, exactly, \"electron\"."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46850,
    "dDurationMs": 4469,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So when someone says \"every time you breathe,\nyou inhale a few of the same electrons that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 51319,
    "dDurationMs": 5540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "used to be in Jesus or Mozart\"… that's about\nas deep as saying that every time you do arithmetic"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56859,
    "dDurationMs": 2710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you use the same number three as Archimedes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59569,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What's more, just like you can call on the\n\"three-ness\" to summon \"negative-three\", which"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63889,
    "dDurationMs": 4061,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has all the exact same properties of three\nexcept opposite and when it meets three they"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67950,
    "dDurationMs": 4670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "annihilate - you can summon \"anti-electron\"\nfrom the electron field and it will annihilate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72620,
    "dDurationMs": 1550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "electron when they meet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74170,
    "dDurationMs": 4019,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Given that electrons are all exactly alike,\nit might seem surprising that they actually"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78189,
    "dDurationMs": 2561,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hate being like each other."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80750,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Electrons despise alikeness so much, in fact,\nthat the universe is forbidden from summoning"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 84530,
    "dDurationMs": 2090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "two or more into the same quantum state."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86620,
    "dDurationMs": 5090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is called \"the Pauli Exclusion principle,\"\nand what it means in practice is that you"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91710,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can't cram too much matter into the same place\n– like a city where building higher than"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 95460,
    "dDurationMs": 4839,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one story is prohibited: instead of skyscrapers,\ncompounds sprawl outwards."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100299,
    "dDurationMs": 4530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So at the most fundamental level, matter is\njust any field (like \"electron\", \"quark\","
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 104829,
    "dDurationMs": 5460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or \"neutrino\") from which you can summon particles\nand anti-particles, but only one at every"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 110289,
    "dDurationMs": 5341,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "point, which means that, quite literally,\nmatter is everything that takes up space."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115630,
    "dDurationMs": 22139,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Like Walmart."
    } ]
  } ]
}
